            </p:TypeAnnotation>
            <p:ValueBoxSettings>
              <p:fontsize p:Type="Int32">40</p:fontsize>
              <p:stringtype p:Assembly="VL.Core" p:Type="VL.Core.StringType">Comment</p:stringtype>
            </p:ValueBoxSettings>
          </Pad>
          <Pad Id="P1Yod0FiLEpOdFq9muE8Yp" Bounds="-471,110,368,229" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="This patch shows how to import an OBJ file.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;An OBJ file contains a mesh. A mesh consists of three&#xD;&#xA;basic elements:&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;• Points (vertices)&#xD;&#xA;• Edges&#xD;&#xA;• Faces&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;vvvv allows you to access these three components&#xD;&#xA;individually. In this example, we will render each of&#xD;&#xA;them separately to understand how a mesh is structured.">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="String" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
